From: Illia Komsa <ik@fungamer.co>
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb: keep the body background off the canvas under
 containment

Document::background_color(), which gives the surface clear color, fell
back to the body's background color whenever the root's was transparent.
It ignored css-contain-2's rule that containment on <html> or <body>
disables the propagation, which the paint path (root_background_source)
already follows, so the canvas outside the root box was cleared to the
body's color. Ask HTMLHtmlElement::should_use_body_background_properties()
first, as the painted canvas background does.

Fixes WPT css/css-contain/contain-{body,html}-bg-001..004 and
css/css-backgrounds/background-color-body-propagation-008/009.
---
diff --git a/Libraries/LibWeb/DOM/Document.cpp b/Libraries/LibWeb/DOM/Document.cpp
index 2460fbc28f..155a3a310a 100644
--- a/Libraries/LibWeb/DOM/Document.cpp
+++ b/Libraries/LibWeb/DOM/Document.cpp
@@ -1721,9 +1721,12 @@ Color Document::background_color(Layout::BegunRead const& read) const
     }
 
     // ...in which case we use the BODY element's background color.
-    if (auto* body_element = body(); body_element && body_element->unsafe_layout_node(read)) {
-        auto color = body_element->unsafe_layout_node(read)->background_color();
-        return color;
+    // https://drafts.csswg.org/css-contain-2/#contain-property
+    // Unless containment on <html> or <body> disables the propagation (the paint path's root background source asks the
+    // same question, so the surface clear color and the painted canvas agree).
+    if (auto* html_element = this->html_element(); html_element && html_element->should_use_body_background_properties(read)) {
+        if (auto* body_element = body(); body_element && body_element->unsafe_layout_node(read))
+            return body_element->unsafe_layout_node(read)->background_color();
     }
 
     // By default, the document is transparent.
